Rectangular plot with approximately eight metres of northern road frontage and 24 metres depth. Public asphalt road, approximately 18 metres wide within a 28-metre right of way. SAM reports orange planning zoning and residential/commercial surroundings.

Material mangrove and title disclosure: SAM reports that the property appears within a 2000 mangrove boundary dataset. Its page cites coastal-authority information about economic zone B and parent deed 23044 issued on 10 May 1973. This is source-reported background, not a title-validity guarantee or unrestricted development entitlement.

The attached two-page SAM notice specifically identifies deed 123145 within mangrove areas under Cabinet resolutions dated 15 December 1987 and 22 August 2000. Buyers must investigate title provenance. SAM sells as-is under current documents without warranting their completeness or lawful issuance; the notice allocates title-revocation risk to the buyer.

The notice includes conditions concerning expropriation, failed transfer, cancellation or revocation of title, SAM cancellation rights, and specified refunds within 30 days after contract termination without interest or compensation. Read the complete notice and verify current deed 123145, its relationship to parent deed 23044 and current restrictions with SAM and the land office before offering.

